IMPORT prelude

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library, and defines no YMD. The Act counts in days ("within 28 days after the day of
-- the order", s 133) and in months ("within 6 months after that death", s 79). A period of months "after" a day ends
-- on the corresponding day of the later month; where that month has no such day (31 August + 6 months), on its last
-- day. The Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic) is not deposited; this is the convention taken (NOTES.md, fork
-- F2). The helpers restate those of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 encoding (a module cannot import
-- across subjects).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Powers of
-- Attorney Act 2014, Version No. 007 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Powers of Attorney Act 2014`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The corresponding day n months after a day (the last day of the month if it has no corresponding day).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the start`) `and` (`the days in month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`)) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS ((DATE_YEAR `the start`) TIMES 12) PLUS ((DATE_MONTH `the start`) MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the target year` MEANS FLOOR (`the month index` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the target month` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the target year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b
